1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,458
The Video Call With Grandma.

3
00:00:03,458 --> 00:00:08,240
Every Sunday, Mom calls Grandma, and we all squeeze onto the couch to say hello.

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:13,469
Today, Grandma can see the ceiling, the top of Dad's head, and absolutely none of us.

5
00:00:13,732 --> 00:00:15,809
Move the camera a little higher.

6
00:00:15,809 --> 00:00:17,622
No, the other way.

7
00:00:17,622 --> 00:00:18,830
There.

8
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:20,840
Now I can see everybody.

9
00:00:21,124 --> 00:00:24,847
Mom is talking to Dad, who is balancing the tablet against a pillow.

10
00:00:24,847 --> 00:00:28,014
Grandma waves on the screen, but we can't hear her yet.

11
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,544
I turned the volume down earlier.

12
00:00:30,544 --> 00:00:32,179
Let me fix that.

13
00:00:32,452 --> 00:00:33,925
Can you hear us now?

14
00:00:33,925 --> 00:00:35,883
Grandma gives us a thumbs-up.

15
00:00:35,883 --> 00:00:39,571
She says she can hear Ben better than anyone, which is not surprising.

16
00:00:39,571 --> 00:00:41,862
He's sitting closest to the microphone.

17
00:00:42,148 --> 00:00:43,777
Hi, Grandma!

18
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:45,433
I lost a tooth!

19
00:00:45,724 --> 00:00:47,405
You don't have to shout.

20
00:00:47,405 --> 00:00:50,436
She's far away, but the microphone is right here.

21
00:00:50,716 --> 00:00:53,314
Grandma laughs and asks us what we've been doing.

22
00:00:53,314 --> 00:00:55,553
Mom points the camera toward me.

23
00:00:55,553 --> 00:00:57,022
What have you been up to?

24
00:00:57,022 --> 00:01:01,001
That's Grandma's favorite question, and this time I have something ready to show her.

25
00:01:01,276 --> 00:01:03,051
Lucy made a poster.

26
00:01:03,051 --> 00:01:05,551
I helped by not spilling anything on it.

27
00:01:05,836 --> 00:01:07,903
A very valuable contribution.

28
00:01:07,903 --> 00:01:11,382
I hold up the poster and tell Grandma about our neighborhood project.

29
00:01:11,382 --> 00:01:14,882
Then Ben shows the gap in his teeth from three different angles.

30
00:01:15,148 --> 00:01:17,067
Same time next Sunday?

31
00:01:17,308 --> 00:01:18,854
Grandma nods.

32
00:01:18,854 --> 00:01:22,750
We wave goodbye, and Dad carefully moves the tablet off the pillow.

33
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:26,281
Next week, we'll try to show her our faces right from the beginning.
